diff --git a/docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md b/docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md
index 3c34d99..4d24845 100644
--- a/docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md
+++ b/docs/PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md
@@ -1032,3 +1032,20 @@ The project is done only when a user familiar with legacy Google Zhuyin can type
 The defining property is:
 
 **The user thinks about the text they want to type, not which language mode the keyboard is currently in.**
+
+## Chinese candidate quality: stored-entry boundary (2026-09-12)
+
+Meaningless generated sequences are quality defects. Chinese decoders must not
+join separate dictionary entries into novel phrase candidates. Native and Java
+fallback implementations must enforce this at generation, rather than maintain
+blacklists or construction-specific ranking repairs. Full, partial, initial and
+mixed phonetics must continue to find stored phrases. Explicit word selection and
+opt-in user phrase learning remain supported. Whole-input phrase choices precede
+shorter consumed-prefix recovery choices without discarding those choices.
+
+Local quality control must assert zero native sentence and Java assembly outputs,
+then report first-line/page coverage losses and gains on frozen corpora. This
+invariant does not establish the semantic quality of every existing dictionary
+entry. Dictionaries still require attributed source audits, and conversations and
+essays require separate coverage reports. Marketing screenshots use real output
+and must be recaptured after defects are fixed; never retouch or tune to hide them.
